<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    OWNER: the replication track, maintained with tools/ by Dev D.

    WHY IT EXISTS

    ClientMessageRouter raises nine events. For most of the project's life THREE of them had a
    production subscriber, and nothing said so: the server framed a death, the client decoded it
    correctly, the router raised OnDeath, and the delegate was null. Every layer passed its own
    tests. The bug lives in the gap between them, where no test was looking.

    This gate closes that gap by asking a question no unit test can ask: does anything in the
    Unity tree actually subscribe? It is the answer to "how do we stop the seventh dead event",
    and the reason it is a tools/ console check rather than an xunit test is plans/replication/
    phases/phase-v10-client-event-consumption.md decision D21 — Assets/Scripts/Net/Client and
    Assets/Scripts/Assembly-CSharp compile into Assembly-CSharp, which has no .asmdef, and CI has
    no licensed Editor, so there is no Unity assembly for dotnet test to reflect over.

    HOW IT WORKS — two halves, deliberately different mechanisms (D21)

      Enumerate the events   reflection over ClientMessageRouter, an engine-free type. Renaming
                             an event changes the gate's input automatically; there is no second
                             list to keep in sync.
      Detect the subscribers Roslyn parse of Ironfront_Reborn/Assets/Scripts. Roslyn rather than a
                             grep for "+=" because Roslyn ignores comments and #if blocks, and a
                             commented-out subscription reporting green is exactly the failure
                             this gate exists to prevent.

    WHAT IT DOES NOT DO

    It resolves no types. "OnDeath += Handler" counts as a subscription to OnDeath whatever the
    receiver's static type is. That is a deliberate over-acceptance: the cost is a missed
    diagnosis on a hypothetical unrelated type that happens to declare an identically-named
    event, and the alternative is a full Unity compilation this repository cannot perform.

    A REGISTRATION MANIFEST WAS REJECTED (D21). A test asserting every event has a manifest entry
    proves the manifest is complete, not that anything is wired.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Ironfront.Tools.ClientWiringGate</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>ClientWiringGate</AssemblyName>
    <Description>Fails the build when a ClientMessageRouter event loses its last production subscriber.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- No Version: Central Package Management (Directory.Packages.props) owns it. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The event list comes from the real type, not from a copy of it. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Ironfront.Net.Replication\Ironfront.Net.Replication.csproj" />
    <!-- G11 derives the announced set from ConnectAcceptedPayload and UdpTransportServer by
         reflection, so it must compile against both rather than restate their shapes. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Ironfront.Net.Protocol\Ironfront.Net.Protocol.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Ironfront.Net.Transport\Ironfront.Net.Transport.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
